          "Engage the college-educated homeowner majority on property tax fairness and municipal efficiency: at $85,000 median household income with substantial college-educated property owners, the district contains fiscally moderate voters concerned about tax burden and government effectiveness; dismissing these concerns as regressive sidelines a voting bloc capable of swing behavior in a closer election.",
          "Do not treat 100% unopposed results as permanent — actively build constituent relationships with specific demographic cohorts: younger renters in the 25–40 age range, Middlebury College faculty and professional staff, and rural landowners in the district's periphery all have distinct concerns that can be addressed through specific legislative focus and constituent service.",
          "Recognize that this district's ideological diversity runs within the Democratic base itself: progressive renters prioritizing affordability and climate action; fiscally moderate professionals concerned with tax efficiency and local control; and rural property owners with distinct land-use and infrastructure concerns represent legitimate internal tensions that will be exploited by any credible challenger who understands the actual composition of this nominally safe seat."
