          "Engage property tax and fixed-cost burden as the primary economic security issue: homeownership at 89.1% and affluence at $96,000 income mask structural vulnerability among voters whose asset values are rising faster than incomes can sustain; challenge Conlon specifically on whether state tax policy is fair to property-owning households.",
