          "Lead with constituent service and local engagement: in a district where 81.9% are homeowners with $69,684 income and a 51.6-year median age, voters evaluate on whether their representative has delivered tangible results on property values, school quality, healthcare access, and municipal infrastructure — not partisan messaging. The incumbent's best defense is a documented record of constituent responsiveness.",
          "Address the 49% opposition directly: understand specifically whether the opposition is concentrated among younger renters and working families (18.1% renter rate), college-educated voters skeptical of incumbent performance, or a combination — and offer concrete answers to their concerns rather than assuming they will stay home or default to partisan alignment.",
          "Develop fluency on property tax, education funding, and healthcare access: these are the three material concerns of a 51.6-year-old, 81.9% homeowner, high-income constituency with above-average college attainment. A representative who cannot speak with specificity about how their voting record and legislative agenda serve these needs is vulnerable to a challenger who can."
