          { name: "Assuming Homeowner Majority Stability Without Demonstrating Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "The three-way tie reveals that despite the district's high homeownership (75.3%), stable age (47.4 median), and affluence ($76,474 income), the natural homeowner coalition has fragmented because none of the available candidates has established credible competence in addressing the specific governance concerns that homeowners actually care about. Any candidate who assumes the homeowner majority will consolidate around generic conservative positioning without demonstrating specific knowledge of Windsor's local challenges will find the constituency remains split across multiple alternatives." }
